```toml meta
cacheable = true
l-space   = "stable"
role      = "bring external content from a source into a bag, carrier by carrier"
tags      = ["lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance", "lar:///carriage.bag.loads"]
title     = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/carriage.bag.loads"
type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/carriage.bag.loads"
```

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.bag.loads ~ the residency LOAD: content from outside the mesh lands in a bag, its provenance named

`LOAD` brings external content into a bag from outside the mesh. Islands never fetch (the web3-only law), so this operator gesture holds the disk grant: it reads the source on the host, derives each carrier's title (a file under a `bags/<holding>/` or `wikis/<slug>/` mirror tree keeps its stable `lar:` name; any other file namespaces under the destination bag by its path relative to the source), and sends the content WITH the verb. A source that does not resolve locally sends a provenance-only LOAD with no carriers (the line says so); an empty file skips with a warning that names it.

LOAD mints a fresh change-id unless `change-id=` names one, since external content carries no prior mesh identity. A terminal asks `Proceed? [y/N]` before it submits; `yes=true` names the intent off a terminal, `mu=pentacle` previews and commits nothing, `in-wiki=true` runs the act in the active wiki's island. Disk memory that already stands in a bag's source tree takes `lares ingest`, whose gate carries the hashes this act does not.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ load-a-directory · preview-first

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`load-a-directory` params=`source-uri/./imports/notes to/lar:///ha.ka.ba/wikis/lares/working ~ read a host directory and land each carrier in the working layer`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`preview-first` params=`source-uri/./imports/notes to/lar:///ha.ka.ba/wikis/lares/working mu/pentacle ~ name the effect and commit nothing`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ source-uri · to · change-id · in-wiki · yes · mu

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`source-uri` params=`takes/path-or-uri needs/required ~ the external content source: a host path, or an address whose provenance the record keeps`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`to` params=`takes/bag-uri needs/required ~ the bag the content lands in`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`change-id` params=`takes/id ~ the change's own identity, named once so a re-send reads as the same change; absent, the verb mints one`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`in-wiki` params=`~ run the act in the active wiki's island`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`yes` params=`~ the intent a call off a terminal names in place of the y/N a terminal asks`>>
<<~ kahea uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance#/takes/mu`>>
<<has entity=`cell` name=`_0` params=`mu/pentacle ~ a dry run: the island walks the act through a capturing access and names the effect it would land, committing nothing`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ write

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`write` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ the vessel checks the writer's cap on the destination bag; a terminal asks y/N before it submits unless yes=true rides, and an agent off a terminal names yes=true`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ usage · cap-denied · outcome-unknown

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[carriage.bag.loads source-uri/<path> to/<bag>]] ~ source-uri= and to= both stand required`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`cap-denied` params=`~ the writer's cap on the destination bag falls short; nothing landed`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`outcome-unknown` params=`~ this process stopped waiting after the vessel answered; a short read found no receipt for this attempt's request id; read it back with lares vessel request <id> before any re-run`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ done · preview · refused

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`done` params=`exit/0 fields/[[verb status requestId receipt]] ~ the vessel ran the action and wrote its effect record; the receipt names the outcome tiddler`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`preview` params=`exit/0 ~ with mu=pentacle the vessel names the effect it would land and commits nothing`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`refused` params=`~ the vessel refused by name (cap-denied or a verb-error); the line carries its reason and cure`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

